{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":137938,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bc24ea37-9a52-42b6-88fc-cf06da382d00","total_cost_usd":0.7116685,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39210,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":11501,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39210,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11501,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39210},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":23475,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.023549999999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11501,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":39210,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6881185000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\":     { \"slots_crushed\": 1, \"slots_uncrushed\": 2, \"hand_tetherable\": true },\n    \"medium\":    { \"slots_crushed\": 2, \"slots_uncrushed\": 4, \"hand_tetherable\": true },\n    \"oversized\": { \"slots_crushed\": 6, \"slots_uncrushed\": 12, \"hand_tetherable\": false }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 36.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded aluminium lattice off a broken solar boom — the bread-and-butter haul of the low sky, cheap per kilo but it crushes flat and never argues on the way down.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"crumpled_foil_blanket\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Crumpled Foil Blanket\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 4.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"Shredded multi-layer insulation that tumbles like a dropped sandwich wrapper — almost free to tow, which makes it the piece a beginner learns the tether on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"burnt_panel_offcut\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Burnt Panel Offcut\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 9.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A scorched honeycomb face sheet torn off a bus panel, already half-cooked by its own decaying orbit and worth taking only because it costs nothing to carry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_bolt_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Bolt Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 6.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 15,\n      \"notes\": \"A knot of frangible separation bolts still welded to their collar — dense little lumps of good steel that Armstrong will always take off your hands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_antenna_whip\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Antenna Whip\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 3.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A hairline-split monopole that glints on a slow cycle across the whole band — the cheapest possible lesson in what fragile costs you, since it weighs nothing and still can't be crushed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_hull_plate\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Hull Plate\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 41.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 7,\n      \"notes\": \"A curved slab of pressure-vessel skin, the heaviest thing down here that a hand magnet will still hold — the first piece that makes the jetpack feel like it's pushing a train.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dented_pressure_bottle\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dented Pressure Bottle\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 18.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A spent cold-gas tank, vented and safe, packing surprising mass into one crushed slot — the best mass-to-slot bargain the low sky offers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_lens_cowl\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Lens Cowl\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 5.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"The glass sunshade off a cheap earth-imager, spidered but intact, orbiting well clear of the common clumps so reaching it is a deliberate crossing rather than a drift.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"collapsed_launch_shroud\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Collapsed Launch Shroud\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 210.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"Half a payload fairing, folded like a dropped umbrella — crane-cable only, so it sits in the sky all semester as a visible advertisement for an upgrade the shipping slice does not sell.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 62.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A cast steel gimbal block with the flywheel still seized inside — the workhorse of the low band, solid enough to shrug off a mediocre landing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"severed_solar_wing_spar\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Severed Solar Wing Spar\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 55.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The load-bearing backbone of an array with the cells sheared away, long enough that it swings wide on every turn and teaches the player to stop before slewing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 28.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A wing panel of intact gallium cells behind fractured cover glass — the signature fragile piece of the slice, four uncrushed slots forever and double damage from every mistake.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"battery_pack_module\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Battery Pack Module\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 78.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A brick of lithium cells in a machined frame — the heaviest hand-tetherable piece in the shipping slice, and the one that decides whether a two-tether string is a good idea.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"thruster_nozzle_bell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Thruster Nozzle Bell\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 24.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A niobium bell off an attitude thruster, dense and compact, the piece that makes a one-slot capture feel worth the crossing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 12.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled optical head the size of a coffee can, light and precious and utterly uncrushable — the cheapest way to learn that fragile is about bulk and risk, not weight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tangled_harness_bundle\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tangled Harness Bundle\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 15.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A snarl of copper loom torn out of a bus, floppy on the cable and forgiving of every rough latch — the low band's filler, and its safety net on a thin run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"parabolic_dish_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Parabolic Dish Section\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 30.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A quarter-segment of a mesh reflector on its own faster orbit, catching the light on a slow cycle — a real ship manoeuvre to reach and a patient closing rate to latch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"derelict_upper_stage_tank\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Derelict Upper Stage Tank\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 380.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A drained kick-stage tank the length of the rocket itself — crane-cable only, and the piece the player circles once, measures with their eyes, and files away for later.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"comsat_bus_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Comsat Bus Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 145.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The machined spine of a dead communications satellite, dense with fittings — the common piece of the top band and heavier on its own than most complete low-band hauls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hardened_avionics_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Hardened Avionics Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 120.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A radiation-shielded flight computer in a lead-lined box, built to survive anything the sky could do to it — which is exactly why it survives the ride down too.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_propellant_sphere\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Propellant Sphere\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 165.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A thick-walled titanium sphere off a station-keeping system, the single heaviest thing a hand magnet will hold at any tier — one of these turns a routine reentry into a three-pass problem.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"momentum_gyro_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Momentum Gyro Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 84.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"Three control-moment gyros still bolted to their pedestal, absurdly dense for one crushed slot — the piece that proves mass, not volume, is what fills the top band's holds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sensor_boom_mast\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Sensor Boom Mast\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 52.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A telescoping magnetometer boom, collapsed and locked — awkward to latch square, but it crushes into a single slot and asks nothing else of the flight home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gallium_solar_panel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gallium Solar Panel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 68.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A full triple-junction wing off a high-orbit bird, worth several solid pieces of its own size class and worth nothing at all if the touchdown runs past five metres a second.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"optical_telescope_barrel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Optical Telescope Barrel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 96.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A mirrored assembly in a carbon tube, heavy and fragile at once — four uncrushed slots, double heat damage, and the best payday in the catalog short of the satellite itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"xenon_ion_grid\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Xenon Ion Grid\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 40.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A pair of etched molybdenum accelerator grids thinner than a fingernail, spawning far off the clumps at real relative velocity — the purest latch-jerk test in the game.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"high_gain_dish_assembly\",\n      \"display_name\": \"High-Gain Dish Assembly\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A full reflector with its feed tower and gimbal still attached — crane-cable only, and the rehearsal piece for the satellite: same technique, forgiving cargo.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"armstrongs_satellite\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Armstrong's Satellite\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1600.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"The one he lost the day of the cascade, hanging above the top band — fragile and oversized, roughly doubling the ship's mass on its own, uncrushable at any tier, and the win condition only if it comes down gently.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 37.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.2,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 76.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 10,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 307.0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mass carries the difficulty curve, because the Researcher says heat cannot. Entry speeds from the three bands differ by only 1,316 / 1,366 / 1,441 m/s, a v^3 heat spread of just 1.31x, so band-to-band difficulty has to come from ballistic coefficient and time spent at heating speed. Hand-tetherable mean mass is 15.4 kg suborbital, 38.0 kg low, 96.3 kg high — roughly 2.5x per band step and 6.3x end to end. Counting the crane-only pieces the plain band means are 37 / 76 / 307 kg, an 8.3x spread. A full hold of high-band junk raises beta far more than a full hold of foil blankets, which is the lever the Researcher explicitly points the crew at.\",\n    \"Fragile fraction is spawn-weighted, not counted, and lands at exactly 0.10 / 0.20 / 0.25. The piece counts tell a different story on purpose: suborbital has 2 fragile types out of 9 (0.22 by count) but they carry weights 5 and 3 against a band total of 80, so the player meets one about one time in ten. The high band has 4 fragile types out of 10 (0.40 by count) weighted 6+5+2+1 against 56, giving 0.25. Counting types would have overstated the low sky and understated nothing.\",\n    \"Every size class and the fragile flag appear in the shipping slice. Suborbital and low each carry small, medium, fragile-small and fragile-medium, so a player who never buys past the hand magnet still meets the whole property space. The three crane-only pieces below the high band (collapsed launch shroud, derelict upper stage tank) exist to be looked at and not taken — visible advertisements for the deferred crane magnet rather than dead entries.\",\n    \"Medium is distributed 2 / 5 / 5 across the bands rather than piled into the top. That keeps the GDD's 'higher bands skew toward medium' true as a proportion — 22% / 56% / 50% of types — without making the low band a small-only tutorial. The slot-cost pressure the high band is supposed to apply arrives through fragility and mass, not through medium count alone.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly best. The dense small pieces (dented pressure bottle, momentum gyro cluster) buy mass efficiency per slot at the cost of a heavier ride home; the light bulky ones (crumpled foil blanket, tangled harness bundle) are free to tow and nearly worthless per trip; fragile pieces pay a premium the Economy Balancer will set but forfeit crushing forever and double every damage source. The greed decision is between axes, never along one.\",\n    \"The two heaviest hand-tetherable pieces per band sit deliberately close to each other — battery pack module at 78 kg in low, cryo propellant sphere at 165 kg in high — so the hand magnet's hold force has a clear ceiling to be tuned against at each tier, and so a maximum tether string of the band's worst pieces is the specific case the Playtester should sweep for shear and for pass count.\",\n    \"Armstrong's satellite is authored into the high band at 1,600 kg because the GDD places it above the top band and there is no fourth band name to use. It is fragile and oversized — the worst combination — with spawn weight 1, so it contributes 0.018 of the high band's spawn weight and does not distort the fragile gradient. Treat its band field as a bookkeeping placement, not a spawn location; it is a fixed object, not a member of the loot table.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":65280,"ttft_stream_ms":1880,"time_to_request_ms":235,"type":"result","duration_ms":136034,"uuid":"5735d38e-d256-474b-9b13-4d554d66c4b6"}
